{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers","id":1509365,"title":"Hekau for Sorcerers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-23T05:36:25-07:00","id":1509365,"title":"Hekau for Sorcerers","content":"This is my attempt to convert Mummy Hekau into sorcerous paths compatible with S20. The goal here is to provide some crunch to mortal members of the Cult of Isis, Children of Osiris, and on the other side the various cults of Bane Mummies.<br /> <br /> <b>Alchemy</b> and <b>Amulets</b> are already covered by their respective Paths (with <b>Enchantment</b> for the latter), so I didn\u2019t see a reason to create new ones. The rituals given in the Mummy rules make some good example spells, though.<br /> <br /> For <b>Celestial</b>, I tried a few different things. Invoking celestial powers, a general buff based on astrology, and so forth. The results were either underwhelming, boring, insanely complex, or some variation where <b>Weather Control</b>, <b>Divination</b>, and <b>Fortune</b> ended up as Aspects of the Path. I don\u2019t like this for linear magic. It should do <i>one</i> thing and increase in power with proficiency.<br /> So rather than re-invent the wheel it makes more sense to just use those Paths as-is, with Astrology as Casting Ability.<br /> <br /> <b>Necromancy</b> is in a somewhat similar spot, as it has aspects of <b>Ephemera</b>, <b>Necromancy</b> (duh), and <b>Starlight</b>. The remaining powers are very specific to Mummies in that they deal with dying and reviving, something that obviously doesn\u2019t apply for mortal Sorcerers. I flirted a bit with a version that grants command over the different parts of the soul as per the ancient Egyptian understanding of it, but again ended up with mostly emulating powers of the above Paths. A specific Casting Ability (for example, Egyptian Thantology) makes more sense.<br /> <br /> <br /> For <b>Ushabti</b>, I plundered the <b>A</b><b>khu</b> version of the same name in <i>Blood Sacrifice: </i><i>the Thaumaturgy Companion</i> p.27, 28<br /> The conversion was ridiculously easy, and the lack of Vitae in the procedure is more than compensated by the increased difficulty from introducing additional Aspects.<br /> <br /> <b>Aspects</b>: Agency, Realism, Time Period (from Divination) as Duration<br /> <br /> <b>Agency</b> (Attributes of created Ushabti as described in BS:tTC)<br /> <br /> \u2022 Laborer<br /> \u2022\u2022 Servitor<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Guard<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Overseer<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Gift of Khnum<br /> <br /> <b>Realism</b> (As per extra success table on p.28 in BS:tTC)<br /> <br /> \u2022 Crude<br /> \u2022\u2022 Fairly realistic<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Moderately lifelike (difficulty 6 to detect)<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Incredibly lifelike (difficulty 8 to detect)<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Indistinguishable from life<br /> <br /> Finally, <b>Ren-Hekau</b> is perhaps the most interesting Path to convert. It cheats as linear magic a bit in that its effects can be very versatile if used creatively, something which I like. At the same time, its scope is limited by the knowledge of <b>True Name</b><b>s</b> the Sorcerer has. Discovering a True Name requires intensive study of a subject, research, and practice.<br /> In game terms, a Sorcerer has to have a minimum level in a corresponding Ability to learn a new Name (eg. Animal Ken for \u201cDog\u201d). The XP invested in the Ability reflect the time invested in study of the subject, the minimum threshold is the level of the Names Aspect.<br /> Additionally, command of True Names gets more difficult the more complex the target of the spell is. Names for simple things are equally simple, but the True Name of a person can be much more difficult to command.<br /> <br /> To use the Path, a sorcerer forms a simple command using words of power and the True Name of the target together with a Command (\u201cEarl Grey, become Hot!\u201d).<br /> <br /> <b>Aspects</b>: Names, Command, Duration<br /> <br /> <b>Names</b><br /> <br /> \u2022 Simple things \u2013 Stone, metal, liquids, a book etc.<br /> \u2022\u2022 Plants and fungi<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Animals and machines<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Humans \u2013 every individual has their own True Name, but parts of their anatomy (\u201cHeart\u201d) may share a common one<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Ephemeral and Supernatural beings \u2013 as above<br /> <br /> <b>Command</b><br /> <br /> \u2022 Change a simple attribute \u2013 Temperature, size, mood, color etc.<br /> \u2022\u2022 Learning the secrets \u2013 Discover hidden characteristics, flaws, or motivations of the target<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Borrow an attribute \u2013 Gain a characteristic from the commanded thing. \u201cStone\u201d skin, \u201cDog\u201d hearing, \u201cJ.R. Dobbs\u201d face etc<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Compel into action \u2013 Force a target into an action (if able), similar to Dominate 2. Also works on non-living things to an extent (\u201cCar, drive forward!\u201d).<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Create something into or erase something from existence.<br /> <br /> <br /> Ideas and criticisms are welcome. This isn\u2019t set out as strictly for NPCs, but also something for my PCs to discover and learn if they are interested.<br /> <br /> I would especially welcome ideas for more interesting Celestial and Necromancy Paths, because just splitting them into their components still feels a bit like a wasted opportunity to me.<br /> \u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 04-23-2023, 08:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T00:35:42-07:00","id":1509459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers#post1509365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is my attempt to convert Mummy Hekau into sorcerous paths compatible with S20. The goal here is to provide some crunch to mortal members of the Cult of Isis, Children of Osiris, and on the other side the various cults of Bane Mummies.<br /> <br /> <b>Alchemy</b> and <b>Amulets</b> are already covered by their respective Paths (with <b>Enchantment</b> for the latter), so I didn\u2019t see a reason to create new ones. The rituals given in the Mummy rules make some good example spells, though.<br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>What does it take to learn these Sorcery Paths ? Is it at all possible for a Sorcerer who is not directly involved with the groups you mentioned in your opening post ?<br /> <br /> It is interesting, nice, curious, and good to see this section of the World of Darkness being used, mentioned and discussed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T02:58:15-07:00","id":1509463,"title":"","content":"Hekau is simply the old Egyptian word for magic and is used as an umbrella term for spells of that tradition. Awakened Magick is referred to as Ra-Hekau in the books. Mummy Hekau are neither Sorcery nor True Magick as described in Mage, but more akin to linear magic. They have access to their own Quintessence flavor called Sekhem, but can't learn True Magick.<br /> <br /> That said, Hekau as a mortal Sorcery does not differ from any other tradition in that a Sorcerer with access to grimoires or teachers can learn it. In fact, one of the core tasks of the Cult of Isis is to teach it to new Mummies, which wouldn't be possible if there was no mortal equivalent. The books never spelled them out, but Sorcerer Revised had a short paragraph about it.<br /> <br /> Seeing how ancient Egyptian grimoires are readily available for anyone interested in real life, I don't think direct involvement with those groups would be strictly necessary for a WoD denizen to learn them. But like with most specialized groups, they would probably have access to better learning resources. Other local factions that could have deeper insight would be the Followers of Set and Bubasti.<br /> <br /> I should also mention that despite the names of the Paths, none of them are exclusive to the Egyptian magic tradition. Ushabti exist in other forms all over the world, and Naming magic is one of the oldest forms of Sorcery that probably started with the development of language.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T05:06:11-07:00","id":1509468,"title":"","content":"There's a book in <i>Storyteller's Vault </i>called <b>Pillars of Ma'at</b> which is designed as an update guide for <b>Mummy: the Resurrection</b>, bringing it up to date with the 20th Anniversary gamelines (which it refers to as \u201cfourth edition games\u201d). Chapter One addresses the Hekau, including a comparison between them and mortal Paths, as well as between them and vampiric Thaumaturgy. Chapter Two addresses the Children of Osiris, including character creation rules for them. They're mostly mortal, with a handful of immunities (to the Embrace, The Veil, Delirium, etc., as well as to non-supernatural diseases), and a perhaps heightened ability to develop psychic numina or to learn hedge magic.<br /> <br /> Chapter Three covers the Cult of Isis, who are described as using an ancient Egyptian flavor of True Faith \u2013 namely, Ma'at. Having Ma'at allows them access to Miracles the same way that True Faith does in <b>Hunters Hunted 2</b>; and the Spell of Life is described in this supplement as a Miracle that's available at Ma'at level 3 or 4, depending on who you're resurrecting. But it also lets them learn and use Hekau (spending Willpower instead of Sekhem), which conceptually separates the Hekau from Hedge Magic: it's more of an elaboration of (one particular flavor of) True Faith rather than being a kind of Sorcery. <br /> <br /> On the other hand, the <i>Storyteller's Vault </i>supplement <b>Sorcerer: Paths of Power</b> (the direct inspiration for <b>M20 Sorcerer</b>) describes both the Children of Osiris and the Cult of Isis as sorcerous orders, with the former specializing in Alchemy and Summoning, Binding, and Warding (Ghosts) while the latter get Alchemy, Divination (Astrology), Enchantment (primarily amulets and statues), and sometimes Healing. In contrast to <b>Pillars of Ma'at</b>, this book suggests that it's probably the <i>Children of Osiris</i> who can learn Hekau. <br /> <br /> Of the two books, I prefer <i>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</i><b>Pillars of Ma'at</b>'s take on mortals learning Hekau; though I might supplement that with allowing the Cult of Isis to take what <b>Sorcerer: Paths of Power</b> calls the Techn\u00ea Background, and which <b>Sorcerer Revised</b> called the Mana Background, and to use that to fuel their Hekau instead of Willpower.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T09:52:21-07:00","id":1509486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers?p=1509468#post1509468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Chapter Three covers the Cult of Isis, who are described as using an ancient Egyptian flavor of True Faith \u2013 namely, Ma'at. Having Ma'at allows them access to Miracles the same way that True Faith does in <b>Hunters Hunted 2</b>; and the Spell of Life is described in this supplement as a Miracle that's available at Ma'at level 3 or 4, depending on who you're resurrecting. But it also lets them learn and use Hekau (spending Willpower instead of Sekhem), which conceptually separates the Hekau from Hedge Magic: it's more of an elaboration of (one particular flavor of) True Faith rather than being a kind of Sorcery.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an attractive alternative- I very much like the idea of Ma'at as basis for True Faith. That would also indicate there is a counter-part surrounding Bane Mummies (possibly with Apep as the opposite number). I'm personally biased towards Sorcery because it's my favorite Numina mechanic, and I also have two active players who play Sorcerers.<br /> <br /> Funny enough, but I would imagine Bardo more as something that is based on Faith than Hekau. But old magic and faith tends to blur a lot anyways.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T11:46:43-07:00","id":1509505,"title":"","content":"Think of it as a unique type of sorcery that's enabled by True Faith. It uses the same mechanics as Hekau, after all, which closely match sorcery with the exception of the True Faith requirement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T22:51:11-07:00","id":1509689,"title":"","content":"There was something similar in the Society of Leopold sourcebook <i>The Inquisition</i> back in VtM 2nd Edition. <b>Theurgy</b> was sorcery paths empowered by the Christian faith rather than pagan spirits or occult science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T03:35:11-07:00","id":1509702,"title":"","content":"Kind of. The main difference is that you didn't actually <i>need</i> True Faith to learn Theurgy; whereas the proposal here is to replace Balance with True Faith (Ma'at) as a cap on what Hekau you can learn (and for whatever other ways that Balance interacts with Hekau).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-26T12:26:21-07:00","id":1509760,"title":"","content":"Historically, Theurgy used to be one of the main modes of magic. You would invoke a deity or deities and ask for their power to fuel the spell: <a href=\"https://books.google.de/books?id=3n595HVp9BMC&amp;lpg=PP1&amp;hl=de&amp;pg=PA158#v=onepage&amp;q&amp;f=false\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>'s one from as far back as ~1000 BCE. Some of the older spells I know are little more than long recitals of secret names (where we cross over with Naming magic again).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers?p=1509505#post1509505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think of it as a unique type of sorcery that's enabled by True Faith.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's perhaps the best way to look at it mechanically- since the power source shifts from the caster to an invoked deity, you need the Faith in order for it to work. At which point a spell becomes (in game terms) a miracle is probably a point of debate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}